OK.  One more time:

you (a)pply FIGURINES to have them turn into monsters.  whether they are
pets or not depends on the blessed/cursed status of the figurine:
	blessed	= pet   (always)
	uncursed = pet  (definately usually, but I think always.)
	cursed = hostile (always)

STATUES, on the other hand, should be broken up by digging into them with
a pick-axe (or wand of striking, or spell of force bolt).  There's a
possibility of a spellbook (or more) inside.  That's the only use I've seen
for statues.  Also, to add to the confusion, there are 'statue traps'
that come to life the first time you either step on their square or try
to break them apart.

I hope this clears the confusion up for you.

